meta {
	name: ConcurrentRequestCreation
	seq: 12
}

auth {
	mode: inherit
}

docs {
	# Creating requests at the same time (#3931, #3937)

	When a requester sends requests for different packages at the same time, each request queues
	the same pending notification to the approver. The calls collide on the outbox
	(`uq_outboxmessage_refid_pending`), and the losing call has to retry and add its package to
	the notification the other call committed (`SaveChangesWithOutboxRetry`, #3937). These
	scenarios check in a deployed environment that both calls succeed and both requests are
	created. A 500 means the retry is broken.

	Duplicate requests from the same request sent several times at once are not covered: they
	do not cause technical errors, and handling them is not part of #3931.

	Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
	`NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. A scenario starts from a known
	state, withdraws what it created, and can run standalone or repeatedly.

	## Parallel calls

	The Bruno runner sends the requests of a collection one after another, so the WHEN step sends
	the calls from its pre-request script with axios and `Promise.all`, over connections opened
	beforehand so they reach the server together. The request of the WHEN step itself only lists
	the pending requests afterwards. Collisions depend on timing, so a passing run makes a broken
	retry unlikely but does not rule it out.

	## Environments

	The Azure DevOps post-deployment run executes the whole `test` folder in every environment.
	Every step starts with `skipOutsideEnabledEnvironments()` from `helpers.js`, which skips the
	request outside `enabledEnvironments`: where AccessManagement.Enduser.RequestV2Api is on and
	the seed data is verified.

	## Tokens and fixtures

	Personas live in `testdata/delegationrequest-scenarios/<tokenEnv>.js` under
	`concurrentRequestCreation`, from the `be-om-tilgang` fixtures. The requester is an
	organisation acting through its innehaver, the approver a private person connected to it.
	The scenarios clean up by withdrawing as the requester, not by rejecting as the approver, so
	they send no notifications.
}
